WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.901
-♪ Sentence Sneak ♪

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:04.070
♪ Sentence, sentence ♪

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.571
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.041
We'll each get cards
with sentences written on them.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.074
These sentences
are completely random.

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:10.476
All right?
-Uh-huh.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:12.945
-Our goal is to work these
sentences into a conversation

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.781
as casually
and seamlessly as possible.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:17.784
Here are your cards.
Here are mine.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.286
Now let's let
the sentence sneak begin.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.387 line:0%
-One at a time?
-Yep.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.990 line:0%
You look at the first card.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:29.328 line:0%
Now, I'll just say, what do you
love most about the Fall?

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:33.866 line:0%
-Uh, I like, you know,
going out on hikes

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:37.303 line:0%
as the leaves are falling
and hearing, you know,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.138 line:0%
the lovely crunch
underneath my feet,

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.940 line:0%
and I've got quite big feet,
so I've got quite a big crunch,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.144 line:0%
and in that way, I've got
a lot in common with Bigfoot.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.244 line:0%
[ Ding! ]

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.812 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:49.215 line:0%
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.916 line:0%
-Whereas he likes the Fall?
Is that what you're saying?

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.018 line:0%
He enjoys the animals?

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.219 line:0%
-Well, you know,
because he's got big feet,

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.654 line:0%
and so I imagine,
when Bigfoot's walking around,

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.322 line:0%
the Sasquatch, he's gonna --

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.324 line:0%
you're gonna hear
the crinkle and the crackle

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.826 line:0%
of his big hairy feet.
-Crinkle and crackle.

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.360 line:0%
-My feet aren't that hairy,
but they are big.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.429 line:0%
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.299 line:0%
Yeah. And he goes around and --
-He just mooches around.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.133 line:0%
-I don't think --
I think that he --

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.468 line:0%
that he lives in a house.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.171 line:0%
-Do you think he lives outside?
Do you like the outside?

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:13.506 line:0%
-Yeah.
I love the outside.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.174 line:0%
I'd love --
You know what I'd love?

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.176 line:0%
I'd love a tent.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:20.079 line:0%
In fact,
I once asked Santa Claus

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:24.216 line:0%
for a tent when I was a child.

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.951 line:0%
I never got it.

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:27.753 line:0%
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:30.056 line:0%
Yeah, I think Santa Claus
owes me a present.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.057 line:0%
[ Ding! ]

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.292 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.695 line:0%
-You know,
it's strange, that, isn't it?

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.932 line:0%
Just having
a bit of a beef with, uh...

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.433 line:0%
[ Laughing ]

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.667 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:42.968 line:0%
-With Santa Claus, yeah.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.904 line:0%
-Oh, with Santa Claus, yeah,
with Father Christmas.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.940 line:0%
It's just --
Oh, God.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.811 line:0%
It's just, you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:55.547 line:0%
You know, it's oftentimes
that things take me back --

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:57.583 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-What do you mean?

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:58.951 line:0%
Like getting
in a fight with Santa?

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.386 line:0%
-Getting in fight with Santa.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.420 line:0%
Or you know, it's just whenever

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.622 line:0%
people complain
about some things.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.824 line:0%
You know what I mean?
Oh, just sometimes...

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:05.825 line:0%
Well, for example --

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.059 line:0%
-You can talk to me.
I'm your friend.

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:09.495 line:0%
-You sure?
-Yeah, tell me anything.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:13.032 line:0%
-You know,
it's like they say in Wyoming,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.068 line:0%
you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.704 line:0%
weathermen are great dancers.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.704 line:0%
[ Ding! ]

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.407 line:0%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.641 line:0%
-I've heard that.
I've seen --

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:25.178 line:0%
-You've seen them.
-I've seen that uh -- yeah.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.779 line:0%
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Uh-huh.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.181 line:0%
-I don't think
that's such a bad thing.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.215 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.283 line:0%
-I think there's --

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.918 line:0%
I think that
should be on a T-shirt.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.586 line:0%
-I think that
should be on a T-shirt.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.789 line:0%
-And I think that T-shirt
should be a slogan,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.425 line:0%
and I think
that slogan should be famous,

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.093 line:0%
and I think aliens

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.229 line:0%
should be called
Outer Space Boys, you know?

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.497 line:0%
[ Ding! ]

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.866 line:0%
-That's a great name.
You think a lot of things.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.067 line:0%
-I love to think.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.103 line:0%
-Thinking -- Thinking is good.
-I love to think.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.504 line:0%
-And it's sometimes
when you don't think,

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.839 line:0%
that really
exciting things happen.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.507 line:0%
You know, just things
that are left to chance.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.908 line:0%
You know sometimes when you --

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.777 line:0%
For example, you know,
when you've got

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.246 line:0%
your phone in your pocket,
and you just accidentally

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.514 line:0%
kind of butt-dial somebody.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.049 line:0%
I mean, once, I actually
butt-dialed Michael Phelps,

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:06.018 line:0%
and it changed my life.
[ Ding! ]

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.119 line:0%
-How?
How so?

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.422 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-How --

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.089 line:0%
It changed your life?
Why?

00:03:11.089 --> 00:03:12.825 line:0%
Did he pick up the phone?

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.261 line:0%
-Well, before, I used to take in
a lot of water when I swam,

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.695 line:0%
and now --
-Yeah.

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:18.364 line:0%
-Until you almost drowned.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.733 line:0%
-I almost drowned.
Yeah.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.234 line:0%
-I love swimming.
I love any --

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:23.870 line:0%
-What's not to love about
swimming and Michael?

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.305 line:0%
-No, I love swimming.
I love the --

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:28.741 line:0%
the hats and the goggles
and the --

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.942 line:0%
-Yeah.
-...Speedos.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.011 line:0%
-The Speedos.
-Get me in a Speedo and --

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:36.349 line:0%
Get me near a Speedo, and I
break my camera out immediately.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.449 line:0%
-Do you?
-Yeah.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:38.785 line:0%
-Do other people do that?

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.252 line:0%
I mean, do you have
to do that in private,

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.320 line:0%
or is that not a problem?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.988 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:44.457 line:0%
-People want it from me.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.025 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.594 line:0%
People -- People --
People want it from me.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.496 line:0%
-We all want you
in your Speedos.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.730 line:0%
-No. Well, it's for --
Obviously.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.633 line:0%
39 people subscribe
to my fashion blog.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:54.667 line:0%
[ Ding! ]

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:59.471 line:0%
So they all want to see.
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:00.973 line:0%
-39 people.
-39 people.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.676 line:0%
-Almost 40 people.
My mother's not into it, yeah.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.645 line:0%
-I'm glad I don't have a blog.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.080 line:0%
Otherwise, you know...

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.416 line:0%
I find, you know,
the thing I'd probably get into

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.953 line:0%
on a blog would be cooking.
I like cooking, as always.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.255 line:0%
-I hate to interrupt your story.
-Please, tell me.

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:19.559 line:0%
-Would you mind
singing something for us?

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.627 line:0%
-Sure.
-I mean, just -- we'd love --

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.562 line:0%
-Just something?
-We enjoy your singing.

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.831 line:0%
-I know a song.
What is this one?

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.167 line:0%
There's this cool song called
"I Dropped It."

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.702 line:0%
And it goes
a little something like this.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.737 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:35.941 line:0%
-Could we dim the lights?

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:38.177 line:0%
♪ It was late ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.279 line:0%
♪ I was cooking ♪

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:44.116 line:0%
♪ And everything's going fine ♪

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:48.520 line:0%
♪ I got my masher out
to mash my potato ♪

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.791 line:0%
♪ And then it took
a funny turn ♪

00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:56.495 line:0%
♪ Couldn't quite get
the mash mashed ♪

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:59.998 line:0%
♪ Inside the pan on the stove ♪

00:04:59.998 --> 00:05:04.436 line:0%
♪ So I stretched out
like I was tired ♪

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:06.939 line:0%
♪ And that's when it happened,
lo and behold ♪

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:10.242 line:0%
♪ I got mash in my trousers ♪

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:11.611 line:0%
[ Ding! ]
♪ Yeah ♪

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.645 line:0%
-Oh, yeah!
I love it!

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.148 line:0%
-♪ Dropped right in there ♪

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.650 line:0%
-That was the greatest
smooth conversation.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.319 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:21.620 line:0%
Every time.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.322 line:0%
Everybody does something silly.
-So good.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.224 line:0%
-Benedict Cumberbatch
right there.

